.TH OTPME-USER 1 "2025-12-29" "OTPme 0.3.0a120" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-user \- manage OTPme user accounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-user
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIuser\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-user
manages user accounts in the OTPme authentication system. Users are identities that can authenticate to the system using tokens (OTP, SSH keys, passwords, etc.). Users can be members of groups, assigned roles, and have policies applied to control their access.
.PP
Users are identified by their name within the organizational unit hierarchy (e.g., alice, bob, it/admin_user).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS User Management
.TP
.B add \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fIusername\fR
Create a new user account. By default, creates a user with a default token.
.TP
.B del \fIuser\fR [\fIuser\fR ...]
Delete one or more user accounts.
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIuser\fR]
Display user information. Without arguments, shows all users.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List users, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIuser\fR
Enable a disabled user account.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Do not persist new share mounts on hosts.
.RE
.TP
.B disable \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIuser\fR
Disable a user account without deleting it.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B rename \fIuser\fR \fInew_name\fR
Rename a user account.
.TP
.B move \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-acls\fR] \fIuser\fR \fIunit\fR
Move user to a different organizational unit.
.TP
.B touch \fIuser\fR
Re-index the object to fix potential index problems.
.TP
.B auto_disable \fR[\fB\-u\fR] \fIuser\fR \fItime\fR
Set auto-disable time (e.g. "1d" or "09:53 13.06.2023"). Use \fB\-u\fR to disable if unused for the given time.
.TP
.B enable_auto_mount \fIuser\fR
Enable auto-mount for user.
.TP
.B disable_auto_mount \fIuser\fR
Disable auto-mount for user.
.TP
.B enable_admin_access \fIuser\fR
Enable admin access (temporary\-password self\-service) for the user via the SSO portal. Sets the
.B allow_temp_passwords
config parameter and grants the
.B set_temp_password
ACL for the role resolved from the user's
.B admin_access_role
cascade. Errors if
.B admin_access_role
is unset or the role cannot be resolved.
.TP
.B disable_admin_access \fIuser\fR
Disable admin access for the user: clear
.BR allow_temp_passwords ,
revoke the
.B set_temp_password
ACL for the
.B admin_access_role
role, and purge any active temporary password from every token that still has one.
.SS Token Management
.TP
.B add_token \fR[\fB\-r\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-qrcode\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\-mschap\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-destination\fR \fIDST\fR] [\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] [\fB\-\-weak\-password\fR] \fIuser\fR
Add a new token to the user. \fB\-r\fR replaces an existing token of the same name while keeping its UUID (useful when re-running setup).
.TP
.B del_token \fIuser\fR \fItoken\fR
Delete a token from the user.
.TP
.B list_tokens \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fR[\fIuser\fR]
List all tokens assigned to user(s). Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR) and \fB\-\-token\-types\fR to filter by token type.
.TP
.B deploy_token \fIuser\fR \fItoken\fR
Deploy the token (e.g. a smartcard token).
.SS Group Membership
.TP
.B group \fIuser\fR \fIgroup\fR
Change the user's default group. (A user is added to further groups from the group side; see
.BR otpme-group (1).)
.TP
.B list_groups \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fR[\fIuser\fR]
List groups the user belongs to. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Role Membership
Roles are managed from the role side; see
.BR otpme-role (1).
.TP
.B list_roles \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fR[\fIuser\fR]
List roles assigned to the user. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Policy Management
.TP
.B add_policy \fIuser\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the user.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIuser\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the user.
.TP
.B list_policies \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fR[\fIuser\fR]
List policies attached to the user. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR) and \fB\-\-policy\-types\fR to filter by policy type.
.SS User Configuration
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-a\fR] \fIuser\fR \fIparameter\fR \fR[\fIvalue\fR]
Set a configuration parameter. Use \fB\-d\fR to delete (reset to default) or \fB\-a\fR to append the value to a list-typed parameter.
.TP
.B show_config \fIuser\fR [\fIparameter\fR]
Show all configuration parameters.
.TP
.B get_config \fIuser\fR \fIparameter\fR
Show the value of a single configuration parameter.
.TP
.B description \fIuser\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set user description.
.TP
.B language \fIuser\fR \fIlanguage\fR
Set the user's localization language (e.g. "en", "de").
.TP
.B enable_disabled_login \fIuser\fR
Allow the user to log in even if the accessgroup is disabled.
.TP
.B disable_disabled_login \fIuser\fR
Undo
.BR enable_disabled_login .
.TP
.B unblock \fIuser\fR \fR[\fIaccessgroup\fR]
Unblock the user for the given accessgroup, or for all accessgroups if none is given.
.TP
.B enable_auto_mount \fIuser\fR / \fBdisable_auto_mount \fIuser\fR
See \fISS User Management\fR above.
.TP
.B enable_autosign \fIuser\fR
Enable the auto-sign feature of the user.
.TP
.B disable_autosign \fIuser\fR
Disable the auto-sign feature of the user.
.SS User Scripts
.TP
.B auth_script \fIuser\fR \fIscript\fR \fB\-\-\fR \fR[\fIscript_options\fR]
Set the user's authorization script.
.TP
.B enable_auth_script \fIuser\fR / \fBdisable_auth_script \fIuser\fR
Enable / disable the user's authorization script.
.TP
.B key_script \fIuser\fR \fR[\fIscript\fR] \fB\-\-\fR \fR[\fIscript_options\fR]
Set the user's key script.
.TP
.B get_key_script \fIuser\fR \fR[\fBname\fR|\fBuuid\fR]
Show the name or UUID of the user's key script.
.TP
.B agent_script \fIuser\fR \fR[\fIscript\fR] \fB\-\-\fR \fR[\fIscript_options\fR]
Set the user's agent script.
.TP
.B login_script \fIuser\fR \fR[\fIscript\fR] \fB\-\-\fR \fR[\fIscript_options\fR]
Set the user's login script.
.TP
.B enable_login_script \fIuser\fR / \fBdisable_login_script \fIuser\fR
Enable / disable the user's login script.
.SS VLAN Assignment
A user is never the object of a port authentication -- a token is. So a user
has no VLAN of its own, and cannot be made a member of one. What it can do
is set the default for its tokens through the
.B vlans
config parameter (see
.BR otpme (7)):
.PP
.RS
.B otpme-user config \fIuser\fR vlans \fIvlan\fR
.RE
.PP
A token without a
.B vlans
parameter of its own inherits this one, the same way it inherits any other
config parameter from its user, its unit and its site.
.PP
It only decides where no VLAN of the site answering the RADIUS request names
the token or a role it is in, because membership always wins. To give a
person a VLAN that way, put their token or one of their roles into it (see
.BR otpme-vlan (1)).
.SS Cryptographic Keys
.TP
.B gen_keys \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fIuser\fR
Generate the user's sign and encrypt RSA key pairs.
.TP
.B del_keys \fIuser\fR
Delete the user's cryptographic keys.
.TP
.B gen_cert \fR[\fB\-\-stdin\-pass\fR] \fIuser\fR
Generate a certificate for the user.
.TP
.B key_mode \fIuser\fR \fImode\fR
Set key mode (\fBclient\fR or \fBserver\fR).
.TP
.B get_key_mode \fIuser\fR
Display current key mode.
.TP
.B get_sign_key_type \fIuser\fR
Show the user's sign key type.
.TP
.B get_enc_key_type \fIuser\fR
Show the user's encrypt key type.
.TP
.B key_cache_time \fIuser\fR \fItime\fR
Set how long otpme-agent may cache the users private key, e.g. how long it keeps the yubikey PIV handler open after the PIN was entered. Accepts a plain number of seconds or a time string such as \fI5m\fR. The default \fI0\fR means no timeout, the key stays cached as long as the agent runs. The agent gets the value with the login session, so a change takes effect on the next login.
.TP
.B key_pass \fIuser\fR
Change key passphrase.
.TP
.B sign_private_key \fIuser\fR \fIprivate_key\fR
Set the user's sign private key.
.TP
.B encrypt_private_key \fIuser\fR \fIprivate_key\fR
Set the user's encrypt private key.
.TP
.B sign_public_key \fIuser\fR \fIpublic_key\fR
Set the user's sign public key.
.TP
.B encrypt_public_key \fIuser\fR \fIpublic_key\fR
Set the user's encrypt public key.
.TP
.B import_sign_key \fR[\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-\-stdin\-key\fR] \fIuser\fR \fR[\fIprivate_key_file\fR]
Import the user's sign RSA key. \fB\-n\fR stores the private key unencrypted, \fB\-\-server\fR keeps it on the server.
.TP
.B import_encrypt_key \fR[\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-\-stdin\-key\fR] \fIuser\fR \fR[\fIprivate_key_file\fR]
Import the user's encrypt RSA key. Flags as for
.BR import_sign_key .
.TP
.B dump_sign_key \fR[\fB\-p\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-\-stdin\-pass\fR] \fIuser\fR
Dump the user's sign key to stdout. \fB\-p\fR dumps the private key (or a pointer to it), \fB\-n\fR dumps it unencrypted if possible.
.TP
.B dump_encrypt_key \fR[\fB\-p\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-\-stdin\-pass\fR] \fIuser\fR
Dump the user's encrypt key to stdout. Flags as for
.BR dump_sign_key .
.SS Object Changelog
.TP
.B changelog \fIuser\fR
Show the object's changelog (chronological list of changes with author, timestamp and optional custom text passed via \fB\-\-changelog\fR).
.TP
.B edit_changelog \fIuser\fR \fIchangelog_id\fR
Open the given changelog entry in the editor named by \fBEDITOR\fR to edit its custom text.
.TP
.B del_changelog \fIuser\fR \fIchangelog_id\fR
Remove a single entry from the object's changelog.
.TP
.B clear_changelog \fIuser\fR
Clear the object's entire changelog.
.SS ACL Management
.TP
.B add_acl \fIuser\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR
Add an access control entry.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIuser\fR \fIacl\fR
Remove an access control entry.
.TP
.B show_acls \fIuser\fR
Display all ACLs for the user.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIuser\fR
Enable ACL inheritance from parent objects.
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIuser\fR
Disable ACL inheritance.
.SS LDAP Integration
.TP
.B add_attribute \fR[\fB\-i\fR \fIposition\fR] \fIuser\fR \fIattribute\fR=[\fIvalue\fR]
Add an LDAP attribute to the user. Use \fB\-i\fR to insert a multi-value attribute at the given zero-based position.
.TP
.B del_attribute \fIuser\fR \fIattribute\fR=\fIvalue\fR
Remove an LDAP attribute from the user.
.TP
.B modify_attribute \fIuser\fR \fIattribute\fR \fIold_value\fR \fInew_value\fR
Change an LDAP attribute value.
.TP
.B add_object_class \fIuser\fR \fIclass\fR
Add an LDAP object class to the user.
.TP
.B del_object_class \fIuser\fR \fIclass\fR
Remove an LDAP object class from the user.
.TP
.B show_ldif \fIuser\fR
Display LDAP LDIF representation of the user.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIuser\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form user info text. If
.I info
is omitted, the current info text is opened in the editor specified by the
.B EDITOR
environment variable.
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIuser\fR
Dump the user info text to stdout.
.SS Extension Management
.TP
.B add_extension \fIuser\fR \fIextension\fR
Add an extension to the user.
.TP
.B remove_extension \fIuser\fR \fIextension\fR
Remove an extension from the user.
.SS User Photo
.TP
.B photo \fIuser\fR \fIimage_path\fR
Set the user's photo (JPEG).
.TP
.B dump_photo \fIuser\fR
Dump the user's photo as base64 to stdout.
.TP
.B del_photo \fIuser\fR
Remove the user's photo.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIuser\fR
Export user configuration. Use \fB\-\-password\fR to encrypt.
.TP
.B remove_orphans \fIuser\fR
Remove orphaned object references.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS User Creation Options
.TP
.B \-\-group \fIGROUP\fR
Set the default group of the user.
.TP
.B \-\-groups \fIGROUP1,GROUP2\fR
Add user to multiple groups during creation.
.TP
.B \-\-role \fIROLE\fR
Assign role during user creation.
.TP
.B \-\-roles \fIROLE1,ROLE2\fR
Assign multiple roles during user creation.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Set initial password during user creation.
.TP
.B \-\-weak\-password
Accept a password even if the password policy would reject it. Needs the
.B force_password
ACL on the target unit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-default\-token
Do not create a default token for the user.
.TP
.B \-\-default\-token \fINAME\fR
Specify name for the default token (default: "login").
.TP
.B \-\-default\-token\-type \fITYPE\fR
Specify type for the default token (default: system default).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-qrcode
Do not generate default token QR code (TOTP/HOTP only).
.TP
.B \-\-mode \fIMODE\fR
Mode for the default token (TOTP/HOTP only). See
.BR otpme-token (1)
for the difference between
.B mode1
and
.BR mode2 .
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-template
Create user as a template object.
.TP
.B \-\-template \fINAME\fR
Use specified template when creating user.
.TP
.B \-\-attributes \fIATTR1=VAL1,ATTR2=VAL2\fR
Set LDAP attributes during user creation.
.SS Key Generation Options
.TP
.B \-b \fIBITS\fR
Specify key length in bits (default: 4096).
.TP
.B \-\-server
Generate server-mode keys.
.TP
.B \-\-pass\-hash\-type \fITYPE\fR
Specify password hash type.
.TP
.B \-n
Do not encrypt the private key.
.TP
.B \-\-stdin\-pass
Read passphrase from stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-stdin\-key
Read key from stdin.
.SS Display Options
.TP
.B \-a
Show all users (across all units).
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-show\-templates
Include template users in output.
.TP
.B \-z \fISIZE\fR
Limit output size.
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIFIELD1,FIELD2\fR
Display only specified fields.
.TP
.B \-\-policy\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of policies shown.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of items shown per object.
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by \fIFIELD\fR
Sort output by field.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Output without headers/borders.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output as CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-sep \fISEP\fR
CSV separator character.
.TP
.B \-\-attribute \fIATTR\fR
Display specific attribute in list command.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-acls
Preserve ACLs when moving user.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for encrypting exports.
.SH CONFIG PARAMETERS
Configuration parameters can be set with the \fBconfig\fR command and displayed with \fBshow_config\fR.
For a complete description of all available parameters and their applicable object types, see
.BR otpme (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Creating Users
.TP
.B otpme-user add alice
Create user alice with default token
.TP
.B otpme-user add \-\-no\-default\-token bob
Create user bob without a default token
.TP
.B otpme-user add \-\-default\-token\-type totp charlie
Create user charlie with a TOTP token
.TP
.B otpme-user add \-\-group admins \-\-role ADMIN dave
Create admin user dave
.TP
.B otpme-user add \-\-groups users,developers \-\-roles DEV,USER eve
Create user eve with multiple groups and roles
.SS Managing Groups and Roles
.TP
.B otpme-user group alice developers
Change alice's default group to developers
.TP
.B otpme-group add_token developers alice/login
Add one of alice's tokens to the developers group (group membership is granted per token, see
.BR otpme-group (1))
.TP
.B otpme-role add_user DEVELOPER alice/login
Assign the DEVELOPER role to one of alice's tokens (managed from the role side, see
.BR otpme-role (1))
.TP
.B otpme-user list_groups alice
Show alice's group memberships
.TP
.B otpme-user list_roles alice
Show alice's assigned roles
.SS VLAN Assignment
.TP
.B otpme-user config alice vlans guests
Set the VLAN her tokens use where no VLAN names them
.TP
.B otpme-vlan add_token guests alice/totp
Put one of her tokens into a VLAN, which wins over the parameter above
.SS Applying Policies
.TP
.B otpme-user add_policy alice strong_passwords
Apply password policy to alice
.TP
.B otpme-user add_policy alice workhours_only
Restrict alice's login times
.TP
.B otpme-user list_policies alice
Show all policies applied to alice
.SS Key Management
.TP
.B otpme-user gen_keys alice
Generate encryption keys for alice
.TP
.B otpme-user gen_keys \-b 2048 bob
Generate 2048-bit keys for bob
.TP
.B otpme-user key_pass alice
Change alice's key passphrase
.TP
.B otpme-user dump_sign_key alice
Dump alice's sign public key
.SS Managing User Status
.TP
.B otpme-user disable alice
Temporarily disable alice's account
.TP
.B otpme-user enable alice
Re-enable alice's account
.TP
.B otpme-user rename alice alice_temp
Rename user alice to alice_temp
.TP
.B otpme-user move alice it/admins
Move alice to it/admins unit
.SS Querying Users
.TP
.B otpme-user show alice
Show detailed information about alice
.TP
.B otpme-user list
List all users in current unit
.TP
.B otpme-user list \-a
List all users in all units
.TP
.B otpme-user list "^admin.*"
List users starting with "admin"
.TP
.B otpme-user show \-\-fields name,uid,groups
Show users with specific fields
.SS Using Templates
.TP
.B otpme-user add \-t developer_template
Create a user template for developers
.TP
.B otpme-user add \-\-template developer_template bob
Create bob using the developer template
